Consider $a,b,c\in\mathbb{C}$ such that $\{a-b,a-c,b-c\}\bigcap\mathbb{Z}=\emptyset$ and $v=(a,b,c | a,b+2 |a)$, then \begin{center} \Stone{a}\Stone{b}\Stone{c} [0.2pt] $T(v)$= \Stone{a}\Stone{b+2} [0.2pt] \Stone{a}

\end{center} then $\Omega(T(v))=\{(3,1,1),(3,2,2),(2,1,1)\}$, $\Omega^{+}(T(v))=\{(3,1,1), (2,1,1)\}$. So, by Theorem <<ref:Theorem: basis for Irr generic modules>>, the simple subquotient of $V(T(v))$ containing $T(v)$ has a basis

$$\mathcal{I}(T(v))=\{T(v+(m,n,k)))\ |\ m\leq 0, k\leq m, \text{ and } n> -2\}.$$
